    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0194" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg78"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/873a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May, 6, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the judgment of the Legation, and in the light of the more recent reports from
                    our consuls, how far is the situation in China responsive to the conditions of
                    recognition of governments under international law; and, specifically, in what
                    respects does the Provisional Government still fall short of the
                    requirements?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
